WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.790
Long, long ago, before anyone wrote a single word…

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:12.489
…a grandmother sang to a child. And the song was gone by morning.

3
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.582
People walked across whole continents, carrying songs only in their mouths.

4
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:25.523
They pressed their hands to stone. As if to say: remember us.

5
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.320
Fires became homes.

6
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:30.658
Homes became villages.

7
00:00:30.708 --> 00:00:34.516
Every elder, every story… fading.

8
00:00:34.933 --> 00:00:38.191
Three hundred thousand years of grandmothers.

9
00:00:38.241 --> 00:00:40.599
Almost none of their voices.

10
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:48.859
And now, it's you. On a balcony, far from home, listening.

11
00:00:49.009 --> 00:00:52.324
[Ammamma hums on the phone] Vaavo… vaavo…

12
00:00:52.725 --> 00:00:54.754
This time, you keep it.

13
00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:05.345
[Ammamma hums, clear now] Vaavo… vaavo… vaavo…

14
00:01:07.725 --> 00:01:11.495
The oldest thing we do… a voice, reaching a child.

15
00:01:13.725 --> 00:01:16.446
Kin. Let yours stay.

